# 19.5:9 widescreen (the app's picture format "19.5:9"): the game computes its 3D for 4:3
# (C_MTXPerspective with 1.3333334 in camera.cpp, the culling frustum VIEW_ASPECT in view.cpp, the
# screen-space light projections of the effects, the item / title / sub screen cameras). The app
# shows rows 56..391 of the picture (16:9) in a 19.5:9 box, which stretches it sideways by 39/32;
# with the switch on (re4_core_set_letterbox(2), runtime/core_api.cpp) re4_view_aspect
# (runtime/picture.cpp) gives 4/3 * 39/32 = 1.625 instead of 4/3 in all of them, so the game draws
# (and culls) a wider view that the stretch brings back to the right shape. Off: 4/3, as before.
